-- title:
--   Valuation-one characters factor through the cycle map
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K_0$, and let $\mathcal T$ be the Bruhat–Tits tree [`CerednikDrinfeld.BruhatTits.tree R K₀`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_BruhatTitsTree.html#L83): its vertices are homothety classes of full $R$-lattices in $K_0^2$, adjacency being generated by the relation that two classes have representatives which are adjacent lattices. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field carrying a valuation with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$. Let $G$ be a group acting on the vertex set so that adjacency is preserved, with every vertex stabiliser finite ($hfin$). Let $\tau$ be a $\mathbb Z/2$-valued function on vertices which is $G$-invariant and takes distinct values on adjacent vertices, so a $G$-invariant proper $2$-colouring. Let $E$ be a finite type together with a bijection $eE$ onto the set of $G$-orbits of darts of $\mathcal T$ whose chosen representative has first endpoint of colour $0$. Finally let $\eta : G \to K^\times$ be a homomorphism with $v(\eta(\beta)) = 1$ for all $\beta$ and $\eta(\gamma) = 1$ for every $\gamma$ of finite order. Then there exists $\zeta : E \to K^\times$ with $v(\zeta_e) = 1$ for all $e$ and $\eta(\beta) = \prod_{e \in E} \zeta_e^{\,c(\beta)_e}$ for every $\beta \in G$, where $c(\beta)_e$ is the $e$-th coordinate of [`CerednikDrinfeld.Mumford.pathCycle`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_SchottkyTreeAction.html#L114) at base vertex the standard lattice class [`LT.LatticeTree.stdVertex R K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L358), namely the signed count of the darts of a chosen path from the standard vertex to $\beta$ applied to it that lie in the orbit $eE(e)$ (and $0$ if no such path exists).
--
--   This is the multiplicative, valuation-one ("residue torus") half of the factorisation of a character of a discrete group acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree through the cycle lattice $H_1(G\backslash\mathcal T,\mathbb Z) \subset \mathbb Z^E$, in the style of the period computations for $p$-adic Schottky groups. It feeds the construction of theta quotients in the Čerednik–Drinfeld layer, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.Omega.exists_pairs_v_prod_theta_div_sub_one_lt`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.Omega.exists_pairs_v_prod_theta_div_sub_one_lt) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.Omega.exists_pairs_v_prod_theta_div_sub_one_lt_forall_ne_pmoebius`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.Omega.exists_pairs_v_prod_theta_div_sub_one_lt_forall_ne_pmoebius).
